      "math_academy_id": "e-12452",
      "problem": "Find the value of the vector function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\cos t, \\: \\sin t, \\: t \\right\\rangle$ at $t = \\pi.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t = \\pi$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,\\pi ⟩=⟨-1,0,\\pi \\,⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $\\mathbf f (t)$ at $t = \\pi$ is $\\langle -1, 0, \\pi \\rangle.$\n\nWe can also express the answer using $\\mathbf i$-$\\mathbf j$-$\\mathbf k$ notation or square bracket notation, as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14131015/assets/e54db65e6c7e6d51c1f502de56980c24d85a2458e62aed88ca1f5a77440be880.svg)",
